# Skill Hub local-development template.
# Copy with `task env:init` (or `go -C tools/devctl run . env-init`).
# Values below are local-only placeholders. Keep every secret blank until its
# profile is intentionally enabled; never commit the resulting .env file.

# Core profile: platform and local infrastructure
DATABASE_URL=postgres://skillhub:skillhub@localhost:5432/skillhub?sslmode=disable
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
DEV_CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
COOKIE_INSECURE=1
# Declares this deployment an offline development one. Two things depend on it,
# and the second is why it must stay blank in production: it mounts the offline
# login provider (ADR-020), AND it is the only way a sandbox that isolates with
# the host kernel (isolation `container`, i.e. a node without
# SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=runsc) is allowed to receive a run. Unset, the
# scheduler refuses such a provider and names it in the refusal — which is what a
# production node whose runtime variable went missing should get (ADR-015).
#
# Plainly: with this set, ANY NAME SIGNS IN WITHOUT A CREDENTIAL. There is no
# password, no token and no allowlist on the offline provider — the name you
# type is the account you get. That is the point of an offline provider and it
# is why this variable is the single most dangerous line in this file.
# The API refuses to start when DEV_LOGIN=1 and COOKIE_INSECURE!=1 (added
# 2026-08-29): a deployment that thinks it is production enough to want secure
# cookies is not a deployment that may also hand out credential-free logins, and
# the two variables drifting apart was the only way this could reach a real host
# quietly.
DEV_LOGIN=1
# Clean test mode (M6, ADR-060). Deliberately NOT DEV_LOGIN: `clean` is weaker
# than `container`, and DEV_LOGIN is on almost every developer machine, so
# sharing it would hand "no boundary at all" to everyone. Set to the literal 1
# and three things change together: the scheduler accepts a driver declaring
# isolation `clean` (ADR-059), the object store may be served in-process by a
# carrier that verifies no signature at all, and the database is a single
# connection whose concurrency semantics differ from production. GET /me then
# reports `clean_mode` so the screen can say all three. Leave blank anywhere
# that is not a demo on a machine which cannot install anything.
SKILLHUB_CLEAN_MODE=
OPERATOR_USER_IDS=
# BETA-001 admission list. Unset — the shipped default — means no closed beta
# is running and every signed-in GitHub account is admitted: it can Fork, try
# runs and download. Set to the allowed provider_user_id list (comma-separated)
# to turn the gate on.
BETA_ALLOWLIST=
# Also allows loopback and RFC1918 as import destinations, which httptest and
# compose both need. Never set in production. Link-local (169.254.169.254 and
# the v6 mapping of it), CGNAT, broadcast, unspecified and multicast stay
# blocked even with this on: a development machine has no reason to reach a
# metadata service either (03:INGEST-014).
IMPORT_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
IMPORT_EXTRA_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1
# URL import already works with zero configuration (a built-in host allowlist).
# ENDPOINT and BUCKET fall back to the local SeaweedFS defaults shown here if
# left blank; ACCESS_KEY/SECRET_KEY blank means anonymous access, which only a
# local SeaweedFS accepts. Point all four at a real S3-compatible service and
# its credentials for anything but local dev — otherwise the process fails to
# create/verify its bucket at boot and exits.
OBJSTORE_ENDPOINT=localhost:8333
OBJSTORE_ACCESS_KEY=skillhubdev
OBJSTORE_SECRET_KEY=skillhubdevsecret
OBJSTORE_BUCKET=skillhub
OBJSTORE_SSL=0
LLM_SERVICE_URL=
# Required whenever LLM_SERVICE_URL is set. Shared only by the Go control plane
# and the internal Python LLM service; never expose it to sandbox workloads.
LLM_SERVICE_TOKEN=
METRICS_ADDR=
# The three retention windows below were ratified 2026-08-23 (PDM-006 / 05 R-1a).
# Go duration strings. All three are still fail-closed with no code default: an
# unset value must keep meaning "nobody set a policy", not "use the last number
# someone wrote in an example file".
#
# Download artifact: 30 天. Revised the same day from 一週 (168h), which was
# shorter than the 14-day closed beta it has to survive — a participant who
# packaged on day 2 would find it gone on day 9, mid-study, and the funnel's
# last segment measures exactly that download. NFR-002a rule 1 now states the
# floor: download retention >= the current observation window.
# The sentence that used to end this note — "720h also lines it up with
# PDM-006's 30-day Run Artifact window" — is false as of 2026-08-29: Run
# Artifacts are 90 days now (05 R-11 unified them with TRACE_RETENTION so
# NFR-002a rule 2 is met). Download artifacts stay at 30 days on purpose —
# rule 1's floor is the observation window (14 days), not the re-evaluation
# window, and packaging is idempotent so an expired one can be rebuilt.
# The two numbers are no longer the same number and should not be aligned
# again just because they once were.
DOWNLOAD_ARTIFACT_RETENTION=720h
# Product analytics events: 一年. Ratified LONGER than ADR-029 決策 5's proposed
# 180 days. That ADR argued 180 covers one beta plus one scope review and that
# audit's 400 days was unnecessary; 365 is close to the number it rejected, and
# this is the one data class users produce without submitting anything
# (02:O11Y-004), so the consent disclosure carries 365, not 180.
ANALYTICS_RETENTION=8760h
# 稽核事件保存期（PDM-006 §6 的 400 天）。`maintenance purge-audit` 讀它,
# 未設就拒絕啟動——與 TRACE/ANALYTICS 同一條 fail-closed 規則。
# 400 天 = 9600h。這個 job 在 2026-08-25 之前不存在,而同意書從第一版就
# 對受測者宣告了 400 天。
AUDIT_RETENTION=9600h
# 使用者質性回饋（`feedback_reports`）的保存期。`maintenance purge-feedback`
# 讀它，未設就拒絕啟動——與 TRACE／ANALYTICS／AUDIT 同一條 fail-closed 規則。
# 這一列是 2026-08-29 才補上的，而在那之前 `feedback_reports` 是本 repo
# 唯一一個「已經在收、卻沒有期限、也沒有任何 sweep」的資料類別；它收的是
# 受測者用自己的話寫的 2000 字元自由文字，也就是三類裡最敏感的一種。
# 同批要確認 `GET /policy/data-retention` 真的把它列出來——那個端點原本只列
# 四個 analytics 事件，並逐字宣告「表裡沒有任何自由文字欄位」，那句話對
# `analytics_events` 為真、對這個部署為假。
# 值由 PDM-006 追認（與其餘保存期同一批）。
FEEDBACK_RETENTION=
# Trace event retention. 3 個月 — matches PDM-006's proposal exactly. Required by
# `maintenance rotate-partitions`, which refuses to run without it.
TRACE_RETENTION=2160h
# Skill 刪除寬限期（WS-005／PDM-006 §6.1）。`maintenance purge-deleted-skills`
# 讀它，未設（如下）就拒絕啟動——與上面三個同一條 fail-closed 規則，但理由更硬：
# §6.1 的 30 天「尚未批准」，而這個 job 刪掉的是使用者自己的內容（Skill 與其凍結
# 版本）；被別人 fork、被 Run 用過、或還掛著測試案例的一律不動。要跑就由部署把
# 數字說出來（30 天 = 720h）；沒人簽名之前，刪除完成的畫面也不宣告任何期限。
SKILL_DELETION_GRACE=
# PDM-010 free run allowance. IMPORTANT: unset does NOT mean "off" — unset
# enforces the proposed numbers (20 first window / 30 per window / 5 per day),
# because an unset allowance would leave the platform's only real cost ceiling
# open. `off` is the explicit escape hatch and it disables the display too, so
# no screen claims an allowance nobody enforces (04 乙-2).
# Turned off 2026-08-23 for the closed beta — ADR-055. Per-run brakes are
# unaffected: the gateway key still carries max_budget $0.50 and SBX-013 still
# caps 300K in / 60K out per run. What is uncapped is the NUMBER of runs.
RUN_QUOTA=off

# M5 generation allowance (GEN-004, ADR-047 決策 5). Same asymmetry as RUN_QUOTA:
# unset enforces the proposed numbers (20 first window / 30 per window / 10 per
# day), `off` is the explicit escape hatch and disables the display with it.
# A SECOND variable on purpose — one switch for both allowances would be the
# shared pool ADR-047 決策 5 ruled against, and a generation would quietly eat a
# trial run's balance.
# Turned off 2026-08-23 alongside RUN_QUOTA (ADR-056).
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TURNING GENERATE_SKILL_EXPOSED ON. The sentence that used to
# be here — "the gateway key still carries max_budget" — was true of runs and
# FALSE of generation, and the difference is the whole risk. A run mints a fresh
# virtual key with its own max_budget per attempt (SBX-008). A generation goes
# through the shared static LITELLM_API_KEY, whose max_budget is a cumulative
# deployment-wide balance — so draining it does not merely stop generation, it
# stops /embed, index-time enrichment and every LLM judge with it.
#
# What actually bounds one generation: a 4000-rune description in, a
# 16000-token ceiling (reasoning plus output) and at most two attempts,
# ~$0.0055 with the default mini model. What bounds the NUMBER of them, with
# this off: one in flight per workspace (an in-process gate in skill/admission),
# and — since 2026-08-25 — a per-IP token bucket on POST /skills/generate
# itself.
#
# The sentence that used to be here was the second one on this subject to be
# wrong. It said generation was not one of NFR-001 clause 5's named endpoints
# (true) and that the limiter "still helps because a session comes from the same
# IP it browses from" (false). A token bucket is only debited by the handlers it
# wraps, so a loop that touches nothing but /skills/generate spent no tokens at
# all and the route was, in fact, unlimited. 04 丙-54 was closed on 2026-08-24
# having put the limiter on the three routes clause 5 names, which was correct
# and did not cover this one.
#
# The route is now wrapped for a reason of its own, stated where it is mounted:
# it is the only route on the table that spends money per call. Note what the
# quota cannot do about that — CountGeneratedSkills counts committed
# skill_sources rows, and a generation that fails validation writes none, so a
# loop that pays for the gateway call and is refused every time is invisible to
# the allowance. That is the shape the limiter is for.
GENERATE_QUOTA=off

# ADR-052's hard boundary between 開工 and 曝光. `on` mounts POST /skills/generate
# and GET /skills/generate/failures and makes GET /me list `generate_skill`;
# anything else (including unset) means neither route exists and the web never
# draws the entry point.
#
# The asymmetry runs the OTHER way from the two allowances above, deliberately:
# an allowance left unconfigured leaves the cost ceiling open, so unset must mean
# enforced; an entry point left unconfigured simply is not there yet.
#
# Do not turn this on until 01 §11.2's first funnel segment has a reading. A beta
# participant who meets "搜不到 → 生成一個" is no longer measuring whether search
# works, and that number has one chance with twelve people.
GENERATE_SKILL_EXPOSED=

# NFR-001 clause 5: anonymous search and the two import endpoints sit behind
# a per-IP token bucket (60/min, burst 30 — operational tuning, displayed
# nowhere, so 04 乙-2 does not apply). Unset = enforced with those defaults,
# `off` = none, logged loudly — the RUN_QUOTA convention: a protection left
# unconfigured must not silently be absent. Only `off` is read — any other
# value, a number included, keeps the defaults.
#
# TWO CEILINGS, both real. In-process, so the bound is one API replica. And
# the bucket key is RemoteAddr: behind a proxy or TLS terminator that is the
# proxy, so every user shares one bucket and the cohort is refused together.
# X-Forwarded-For is deliberately not read (a header the client sets is a
# bucket the client chooses); limit at the proxy instead. m4/release-checklist
# §2.3 carries this as a deployment decision. IPv6 is keyed by /64.
RATE_LIMIT=

# GitHub OAuth login. All three are required together (an OAuth App's client
# ID, secret and redirect URL) — without them nobody can sign in unless
# DEV_LOGIN=1 is set instead. Optional when DEV_LOGIN=1. Keep production
# credentials blank here; set them in the real deployment's env only.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=

# Model profile: required only for LiteLLM-backed operations.
# Provider credentials belong to the LiteLLM process only (ADR-017).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# The gateway's admin credential. It stays on the LiteLLM side and nowhere else.
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
#
# READ THIS BEFORE FILLING IT IN. What belongs here is a VIRTUAL KEY minted from
# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY, carrying a `max_budget` and a model allowlist (embedding
# plus the judge/suggest/generate models this deployment actually uses).
# PUTTING THE MASTER KEY HERE IS A DEPLOYMENT DEFECT, not a shortcut.
#
# The master key is not merely "a key with a large budget" — it is the gateway's
# ADMINISTRATIVE credential: it mints virtual keys, reads every key's spend, and
# (with STORE_MODEL_IN_DB on) rewrites model routing. This variable is read by
# apps/llm, a process that handles UNTRUSTED PACKAGE CONTENT AND USER PROMPTS.
# Handing it the master key gives that process the whole model exit. ADR-017's
# decision section says it in one line: "Python 服務與 Sandbox 只持有 Virtual
# Key", and infra/compose/docker-compose.yml repeats it.
#
# This is written here because every run this repository has a record of did the
# wrong thing: m3's suggest-baseline and judge-regression reports, the
# reproduction command in generate_integration_test.go, and 04 丙-56 all set
# LITELLM_API_KEY to the master key. Nothing failed, which is the problem.
#
# Second reason, already stated further up this file: generation and every other
# LLM path share THIS key's cumulative budget. A per-run virtual key drains one
# run; this one drains /embed, index-time enrichment and every judge with it.
# m4/release-checklist §2.3 carries it as a deployment-time check.
#
# Since 2026-09-05 (04 丙-156) apps/llm refuses to start on the master key
# (503 from every model endpoint), and `task dev:llm` mints a scoped Virtual
# Key for it through the gateway's admin API when this is blank or wrong. Leave
# it blank locally; set it only for a deployment whose key was issued by hand.
LITELLM_API_KEY=

# Run and sandbox profile: opt-in and potentially paid.
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_PROVIDERS=
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
# Production MUST be `runsc` (gVisor, ADR-015). Empty means the host's default
# runtime, and the sandbox then honestly declares isolation `container` — which
# only a DEV_LOGIN=1 deployment may be dispatched to.
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_NETWORK=
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:4000
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:4000
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_KEY=
SKILLHUB_RUN_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
SKILLHUB_RUN_MAX_BUDGET_USD=0.50
SKILLHUB_RUN_TPM_LIMIT=200000
SKILLHUB_TRACE_INGEST_URL=http://localhost:8080
SKILLHUB_TRACE_INGEST_SECRET=

# Tests: intentionally blank so normal tests cannot spend money by accident.
# SKILLHUB_TEST_DATABASE_URL needs a separately created test database.
SKILLHUB_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_SANDBOX_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
SKILLHUB_E2E_GATEWAY_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_GATEWAY_KEY=
SKILLHUB_E2E_EGRESS_NETWORK=
SKILLHUB_E2E_RUNTIME_IMAGE=
QA002_CORPUS=
